{{Quote|You are a general. I am a commander. You stand higher in military hierarchy.|[[Senior Captain]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]], undercover as a commander, to [[Jedi]] General [[Anakin Skywalker]]|<ref name="Thrawn: Alliances">''[[Thrawn: Alliances]]''</ref>}}
'''General''' was a senior [[Military rank|rank]] in various [[Army|armies]], including the [[Imperial Army]],<ref name="ESB" /> the [[Grand Army of the Republic]],<ref name="SWDKrell" /> the [[Separatist Droid Army]],<ref name="ROTS" /> the [[Alliance Army]],<ref name="ROTJ" /> the [[Resistance Army]], and the [[First Order Army]].<ref name="TFA" /> Generals were part of an army's hierarchy, as opposed to [[admiral]]s, who had a high role in a [[navy]].<ref name="ESB" /> While some nations in the [[Unknown Regions]] used the rank of general, others used the equivalent title of "[[generalirius]]."<ref name="Greater Good" /> [[Abediah Viess]] led a [[mercenary]] [[army]] of [[Viess's army|warrior-kin]] as a general.<ref name="The Blade 2" /> The [[Unbroken Clan]] syndicate also made use of the rank,<ref name="Aphra 12" /> as did the [[Troik]] tribe of the planet [[At Achrann]].<ref name="Cant Say" />

==History==
{{Quote|Just a little advice, sir. Generals don't apologize. Not for decisions made in the heat of battle. Otherwise you'd do nothing else.|[[Clone Captain]] [[Spider]], to Jedi General [[Thirteenth Sister|Iskat Akaris]]|<ref name="Inquisitor">''[[Inquisitor: Rise of the Red Blade]]''</ref>}}
[[Gungan]] leader [[Rugor Nass|Boss Nass]] was so impressed with [[Jar Jar Binks]]' role in bringing the Gungan and [[Naboo (people)|Naboo]] people together that he promoted Binks to the rank of [[Bombad General]]. The clumsy Binks was one of the [[commander]]s of the [[Gungan Grand Army]] during the [[Trade Federation]]'s [[invasion of Naboo]].<ref name="SWE Gungan Grand Army">{{SWE|groups|gungangrandarmy|Gungan Grand Army}}</ref> During the [[Clone Wars]], the rank of [[Jedi General]] was bestowed on the [[Jedi Knight|Knights]] and [[Jedi Master|Masters]] of the [[Jedi Order]], giving them authority to lead the [[Galactic Republic]]'s [[Republic Military|military forces]].<ref name="SWEbly">{{SWE|characters|clone-commander-bly|Clone Commander Bly}}</ref><ref name="SWEney">{{SWE|characters|clone-commander-neyo|Clone Commander Neyo}}</ref><ref name="SWEyul">{{SWE|characters|yularen|Admiral Wulff Yularen}}</ref> The rank was originally an informal title bestowed upon the Jedi by the [[clone trooper]]s, who wanted a sense of formal military hierarchy in those they fought under, but it was formalized&mdash;along with the [[Jedi Commander]] rank assigned to [[Padawan]]s&mdash;via the [[Jedi Military Integration Act]] passed early into the war.<ref name="Brotherhood">''[[Brotherhood (novel)|Brotherhood]]''</ref>

[[File:Grievous_estaff.jpg|thumb|left|300px|General Grievous, feared warlord of the Confederacy of Independent Systems]]
[[Grievous]] was a feared general of the [[Confederacy of Independent Systems]].<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|general-grievous|General Grievous}}</ref> In the [[Standard month|months]] following her purported [[death]] at the [[Battle of Jakku|Battle]] of [[Jakku]], [[Captain]] [[Ciena Ree]] was nominated for the [[Distinguished Medal of Imperial Honor]] by [[Flight Commander]] [[Nash Windrider]], who explained that he had it on good authority that several [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] generals, [[admiral]]s, and captains also intended to recommend the late Ree for the same award.<ref name="Lost Stars" /> [[Armitage Hux]] was the highest-ranking general in the [[First Order military|forces]] of the First Order, subservient only to [[Supreme Leader]] [[Snoke]] and his apprentice [[Ben Solo|Kylo Ren]].<ref name="TFA" /> [[Poe Dameron]] promoted his friend [[Finn]] to general after the retired General [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] reminded him that they had each other&mdash;and that was how they would win.<ref name="IX">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

